From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:54:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Map the field's error from dropping nodes onto sweep columns

Patch::node_drop gives each dropped node of species 0 and each time band
a light and a soil coefficient, zero in the forward. Each scales the field
change of merging the node's two intervals into one: the spanning
interval's crowns less the two's, with for_each_interval_crown's placement
and summed at the knots through the profile's moments, and per layer the
merged hats' uptake less the two's. The coefficients follow the traits in
ad_parameters(), so the sweep's existing parameter adjoints give the
census's first-order move from each drop, per node and band.

At double the drop is off while every coefficient is zero, and it is off
on a recorded field. The forward and the 50 trait columns are bit-identical
to the build without it, with and without the drop columns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
